# You Won't See Me, bridge (figure 9.2)
# The top row is the six-note descending chromatic line (F# down to C#, the C# landing on the
# downbeat of the next verse). Pollack's 4 3 under the E bars is the 4-3 suspension over V7: spelled
# here as E7sus4 then E7 (my spelling; he writes just E). The G# dim. 7 is in 4/3 inversion,
# D in the bass, as he explains.
#? Octave of the chromatic line (F#4 down) is a guess; Pollack doesn't say which part carries it.
key A

